;; Regulatory source register for JPN-MIC telecommunications-carrier and
;; broadcasting licensing compliance.
;;
;; README.md says: "Every regulatory claim must cite the official MIC source."
;; docs/operator-guide.md requires "clear provenance (official MIC source
;; citation) for every requirement surfaced". docs/business-model.md makes a
;; fabricated regulatory claim a HARD hold that "must be corrected against a
;; cited MIC source first".
;;
;; Until this file existed there was no such list. Three documents required a
;; citation against a set that did not exist, so no claim in this repository
;; could be traced to anything, and nothing could tell a real citation from an
;; invented one. This is that list.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A law not in this table has NO spec-basis for
;; this repository -- extend the table, never invent an id or a URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.cljs`, which re-fetches every entry
;; from the live authority. Each entry carries a :source/verify tag naming
;; WHICH check establishes it. The checks are not interchangeable, and the
;; reasons are the main thing this file has to teach.
;;
;; ── THIS MINISTRY SERVES Shift_JIS AND DOES NOT SAY SO IN THE HEADER
;;
;; Measured 2026-08-27: every page on www.soumu.go.jp answers
;; `Content-Type: text/html` with NO charset parameter, and the bytes are
;; Shift_JIS -- the encoding is declared only in the HTML meta.
;;
;; A verifier that reads the body with `res.text()` gets UTF-8 decoding, which
;; on these bytes produces deterministic mojibake. Measured, for the live top
;; page whose real title is 総務省:
;;
;;   res.text()  ->  title "������"
;;
;; That is not a crash and not an empty string. It is a stable, plausible-
;; looking value, and it breaks the register in BOTH directions:
;;
;;   - Every Japanese :page/must-contain needle fails to match, so every live
;;     page in this register would be reported as a dead citation.
;;   - An author who filled in :page/title by pasting what the verifier
;;     printed would pin the mojibake, and the check would then pass forever
;;     while asserting nothing about the page.
;;
;; So :host/charset is declared per host and the body is decoded with it, and
;; the run re-reads each page's own meta charset and REFUSES if it no longer
;; agrees with the host declaration -- because the day soumu.go.jp migrates to
;; UTF-8 is the day every stored title in this file becomes wrong, and that
;; must not surface as a page failure.
;;
;; Charset is per HOST, not per ministry: www.tele.soumu.go.jp, the same
;; ministry's radio portal, is UTF-8. A verifier hardcoding either one gets
;; the other wrong.
;;
;; ── ON www.tele.soumu.go.jp, "DEAD CITATION" AND "BLOCKED CLIENT" ARE THE
;;    SAME BYTES
;;
;; This is the sharpest thing measured here, and it is why that host carries
;; no page entries.
;;
;; Measured 2026-08-27, sha256 over the full response body:
;;
;;   real page, browser User-Agent     200  29,830 B  a9b3627578b56125...
;;   real page, no User-Agent          403   1,727 B  3559970027daab21...
;;   missing page, browser User-Agent  403   1,727 B  3559970027daab21...
;;   missing page, no User-Agent       403   1,727 B  3559970027daab21...
;;
;; The last three are not merely similar. They are byte-identical, down to the
;; hash: a live page fetched by a refused client and a page that does not
;; exist are the same response. There is no field left to separate "your
;; citation is dead" (FAIL, a claim about this register) from "your client is
;; refused" (REFUSE, a claim about nothing).
;;
;; Sending a browser User-Agent is necessary but NOT sufficient. With the UA,
;; /j/sys/fees/purpose/index.htm answers 200 while /j/index.htm and
;; /j/sys/process/index.htm still answer the same 403 -- so even a UA-bearing
;; run cannot tell which 403s are real. The host is declared
;; :refuses-indistinguishably, page checks on it are REFUSED rather than
;; failed, and the byte-identity is re-measured every run. If the host ever
;; starts telling the two apart, that check is what notices.
;;
;; Note this is a DIFFERENT mechanism from the one this repository family
;; already met on www.mofa.go.jp, where the block is on the TLS fingerprint
;; and curl is refused while fetch is served. Here curl and fetch behave the
;; same and the discriminator is the User-Agent header. Same symptom, and the
;; wrong fix for one is a no-op for the other.
;;
;; ── laws.e-gov.go.jp CANNOT BE CHECKED AS A PAGE AT ALL
;;
;; Measured 2026-08-27 with this repository's own core statute:
;; /law/359AC0000000086 (the Telecommunications Business Act, real) and
;; /law/999ZZ9999999999 (invented) both answer HTTP 200, at the requested URL
;; with no redirect, with the identical title "e-Gov 法令検索" over a small
;; client-rendered shell. Status, final URL and title all agree between a real
;; citation and a fabricated one. The shell's byte length is deliberately NOT
;; recorded: it was measured at 696 and then at 800 bytes within one session,
;; so it moves on its own and pinning it would report the host wrong for a
;; reason that means nothing.
;;
;; So the host is declared :indistinguishable, page checks on it are REFUSED,
;; and every statute is resolved through the law API instead. The
;; indistinguishability is re-measured every run; if the host ever starts
;; telling the two apart, this rule has expired and that is what notices.
;;
;; ── A NEEDLE THAT IS ON THE MISSING-PAGE BODY IS NOT A NEEDLE
;;
;; www.soumu.go.jp's 404 body is a ~39 KB page with the full site chrome
;; attached. Measured present ON THAT BODY, for a URL that does not exist:
;;
;;   総務省   届出   霞が関   100-8926   03-5253-5111
;;
;; 届出 is one of the two entry routes under the Telecommunications Business
;; Act, so "fetch the entry-procedure page and look for 届出" passes on a page
;; that is not there. And 100-8926 / 03-5253-5111 are exactly what
;; organization.edn asserts, so "confirm the HQ contact by looking for the
;; postcode" passes on the missing page too.
;;
;; The verifier does not leave that to whoever writes the next entry. It
;; fetches each host's missing-page body once per run and FAILS any
;; :page/must-contain string found on it, with reason :chrome-needle, before
;; the cited page is fetched at all. A needle that cannot discriminate is a
;; finding, not a detail.
;;
;; ── A REPEALED ACT ANSWERS EXACTLY LIKE A LIVE ONE
;;
;; 特定通信・放送開発事業実施円滑化法 (平成二年法律第三十五号) was MIC's own
;; telecommunications-and-broadcasting development statute and was REPEALED on
;; 2024-04-01. Ask the law API about it today and it answers total_count 1,
;; with the title and the law number matching what a citer would have written
;; down. A verifier comparing only title and number reports PASS for a statute
;; repealed two years ago -- recent enough that an adviser could plausibly
;; still be citing it.
;;
;; The distinguishing fields are repeal_status / repeal_date, declared per
;; entry and re-measured here. It is deliberately NOT remain_in_force: that
;; field reads like the answer and is not. Measured on the Telecommunications
;; Business Act itself, live and in force, remain_in_force is false -- the
;; same value the repealed Act carries. Keying on it would mark every live
;; statute in this register dead.
;;
;; It is carried below as :repealed-statute so it cannot be read as citable,
;; and so the repeal check has a real negative control to drive.
;;
;; ── AND A LIVE ACT CAN FAIL A THIRD WAY THE REPEAL FIELD DOES NOT SEE
;;
;; 特定電気通信による情報の流通によって発生する権利侵害等への対処に関する法律
;; (413AC0000000137) is live: repeal_status is None. But its
;; current_revision_status is PreviousEnforced, not CurrentEnforced -- the
;; revision e-Gov displays is not the one in force. This is the statute
;; formerly titled 特定電気通信役務提供者の損害賠償責任の制限及び発信者情報の
;; 開示に関する法律, renamed in the 2024 amendment, and an adviser citing the
;; old title gets a title that no longer matches while the law id does.
;;
;; So force-status is two independent fields, not one. Both are declared per
;; entry and both are checked, and this Act is the negative control that
;; drives the revision half -- title, number and repeal status all correct, so
;; only the revision field can catch it.
;;
;; ── LAW IDS ARE NOT DERIVABLE AND WERE NOT GUESSED
;;
;; Every id below was resolved through the API. Measured: 電波法施行規則 is
;; 325M50080000014 and 放送法施行規則 is 325M50080000010 -- 電波監理委員会規則
;; is M50080, not the M50001 that 郵政省令 uses, and every derivation from the
;; parent Act's own id returns total_count 0. Eight ids guessed by that route
;; before the API was asked, eight misses.
;;
;; ── PAGE PATHS ARE NOT DERIVABLE EITHER
;;
;; Measured 2026-08-27: of ten plausible soumu.go.jp paths written from the
;; site's own naming conventions, EIGHT answered 404, including
;; /main_sosiki/joho_tsusin/index.htm and
;; /main_sosiki/joho_tsusin/top/tsushin_service/index.html. Every page URL
;; below was read off a live index page, not composed.
;;
;; ── DATES HERE ARE UTC
;;
;; :source/retrieved-at and :coverage/measured-at are UTC dates, matching the
;; commit that carries them. This machine runs JST, so "today" is one day
;; ahead of UTC for nine hours out of every twenty-four -- long enough that a
;; register written in the evening picks up tomorrow's date and lands dated
;; one day AFTER the commit introducing it. A source dated later than the
;; commit that cites it reads as a date nobody measured, which is the one
;; thing this file exists to make impossible. Use `date -u`.
;;
;; ── WHAT :source/covers CLAIMS, AND WHERE IT STOPS
;;
;; Claims stop at the level actually checked: law identity, repeal status and
;; revision status for statutes, and for pages the title and the body strings
;; read on 2026-08-27. No article text is asserted, because no article text
;; was read. In particular NOTHING below establishes which of 登録 and 届出
;; a given operator needs -- that turns on facility scale thresholds in
;; 電気通信事業法施行規則, which is cited here as an instrument and not read.

[
 ;; ── What this register does not cover ──────────────────────────────────────
 {:source/id "register.coverage"
  :source/kind :coverage
  :coverage/entries 23
  :coverage/by-verify {:e-gov-law-id 14 :page-text 9}
  :coverage/measured-at "2026-08-27"
  :coverage/excludes
  #{;; Article text. Nothing below asserts what any provision SAYS -- only
    ;; that the instrument exists, is identified as written, and is in the
    ;; force status declared. A requirement checklist built on this register
    ;; still has to read the provision.
    :article-text
    ;; The 登録 / 届出 threshold itself. Which entry route an operator falls
    ;; under is the first question this repository is asked, and it is decided
    ;; by facility scale rules in 電気通信事業法施行規則. The ordinance is
    ;; cited; the threshold is not established by citing it.
    :entry-route-thresholds
    ;; Radio-station licensing procedure. 電波法 and 電波法施行規則 are below,
    ;; but the operational procedure lives on www.tele.soumu.go.jp, which this
    ;; register cannot check at all -- see the byte-identity note above.
    :radio-station-procedure
    ;; Fee schedules. 電波利用料 amounts and the 資格手続 fee table both change
    ;; on their own timetable and neither is carried here.
    :fee-schedules
    ;; Subnational instruments. Public-sector network and broadcasting
    ;; procurement is very often run by a prefecture or a city under its own
    ;; rules, and none of those are here.
    :subnational-instruments
    ;; Whether a named operator currently holds a registration, notification
    ;; or licence. The procedure pages are cited; no operator's status is.
    :operator-registration-status}}

 ;; ── Host behaviour the page checks rest on ─────────────────────────────────
 ;; Re-measured every run. Every :page-* entry below is only as good as these.

 {:source/id "host.soumu"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.soumu.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :answers-404
  :host/missing-status 404
  :host/missing-title "総務省｜ご案内ページ　－ご利用のページが見つかりません－"
  :host/known-real-path "/menu_seisaku/ictseisaku/index.html"
  :host/charset "shift_jis"
  :host/declares-charset-in-header? false
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-08-27"
  :source/note "Answers a clean 404 for a path it does not have, which makes
                this the one host in the register where a page check can
                distinguish a dead citation on status alone. The catch is the
                encoding: Content-Type is bare text/html and the bytes are
                Shift_JIS, so a body read with the default UTF-8 decoding
                yields stable mojibake rather than an error -- the live top
                page's title 総務省 reads as \"������\". :host/charset is what
                the run decodes with, and each page's own meta charset is
                re-read and required to still agree."}

 {:source/id "host.tele-soumu"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.tele.soumu.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses-indistinguishably
  :host/charset "utf-8"
  :host/known-real-path "/j/sys/fees/purpose/index.htm"
  :host/requires-user-agent? true
  :host/refusal-status 403
  :host/refusal-bytes 1727
  :host/refusal-sha256-prefix "3559970027daab21"
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-08-27"
  :source/note "Carries NO page entries, on purpose. A live page fetched
                without a browser User-Agent, a missing page fetched with one,
                and a missing page fetched without one all return the SAME
                BYTES -- 403, 1,727 bytes, sha256 3559970027daab21... -- so a
                403 from this host is not evidence about the register. Sending
                the UA is necessary but not sufficient: with it,
                :host/known-real-path answers 200 while /j/index.htm and
                /j/sys/process/index.htm still answer the identical 403. The
                run re-measures the byte-identity and REFUSES any page entry
                naming this host. Different mechanism from the TLS-fingerprint
                block this repository family met on www.mofa.go.jp -- there
                curl was refused and fetch served; here both behave alike and
                only the User-Agent moves the answer."}

 {:source/id "host.laws-e-gov"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "laws.e-gov.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :indistinguishable
  :host/charset "utf-8"
  :host/known-real-path "/law/359AC0000000086"
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-08-27"
  :source/note "A real law path and an invented one agree on status (200),
                final URL (no redirect) and title (\"e-Gov 法令検索\"). The
                body length is not pinned -- it moved from 696 to 800 bytes
                within one session. There is nothing left for a page check to
                compare, so page checks on this host are REFUSED and statutes
                are resolved through the API. Re-measured every run against
                this repository's own core statute; if the host ever starts
                discriminating, that is the check which notices."}

